## PHASE 3 — Backend Upgrade to PostgreSQL
*Goal: Replace SQLite with PostgreSQL to handle spatial data, 50-event scale, and ground reporting.*

### 3.1 PostgreSQL Setup

Spin up a local Postgres instance using Docker:
```bash
docker compose up postgres -d  # We will add this service to docker-compose.yml
```

Update `backend/.env`:
```ini
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://cyclonewatch:cyclonewatch@localhost:5432/cyclonewatch
```

### 3.2 Alembic Migration

```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Migrate to Postgres and expand schema"
alembic upgrade head
```

### 3.3 Schema Expansions

New tables to add:

```sql
-- Ground destruction reports from NDRF/field agents
CREATE TABLE ground_reports (
    id          SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    event_id    VARCHAR,
    lat         FLOAT,
    lon         FLOAT,
    damage_type VARCHAR,   -- G0–G11 code
    severity    FLOAT,     -- S0–S4
    timestamp   TIMESTAMPTZ,
    reporter_id VARCHAR,
    verified    BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
);

-- Multi-task ML predictions stored per frame
ALTER TABLE classifications
  ADD COLUMN damage_class  VARCHAR,
  ADD COLUMN severity_score FLOAT,
  ADD COLUMN t12_lat FLOAT, t12_lon FLOAT,
  ADD COLUMN t24_lat FLOAT, t24_lon FLOAT;
```

### 3.4 New API Endpoints

- `POST /api/reports` — Submit a ground destruction report
- `GET /api/reports/{event_id}` — Fetch all verified reports for map overlay
- `GET /api/replay/{event_id}?source=isro|nasa` — Dual data source toggle
- `GET /api/coastline/distance?lat={lat}&lon={lon}` — Geodesic distance to coast

